 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Suppose you’re about to draw one card from a deck containing only these 10 cards:<br> \n<span data-math=\"{\\text{A}}♡\">{\\text{A}}♡</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{A}}♠\">{\\text{A}}♠</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{A}}♣\">{\\text{A}}♣</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{AA}}\\diamondsuit\">{\\text{AA}}\\diamondsuit</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{K}}♠\">{\\text{K}}♠</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{K}}♣\">{\\text{K}}♣</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{Q}}♡\">{\\text{Q}}♡</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{Q}}♠\">{\\text{Q}}♠</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{J}}♡\">{\\text{J}}♡</span>, <span data-math=\"{\\text{J}}♠\">{\\text{J}}♠</span>. If appropriate, use the Addition Rule to find the probability that one or the other of these events occurs:",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 516386,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"E\">E</span> is the event “the card is an ace” and <span data-math=\"F\">F</span> is the event “the card is a king.”",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{{10}} + \\frac{2}{{10}} = \\frac{3}{5}\">\\frac{4}{{10}} + \\frac{2}{{10}} = \\frac{3}{5}</span>\n\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample Space:</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A heart</td>\n<td>A spade</td>\n<td>A club</td>\n<td>A diamond</td>\n<td>K spade</td>\n<td>K club</td>\n<td>Q heart</td>\n<td>Q spade</td>\n<td>J heart</td>\n<td>J spade</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>There are 10 cards, 4 of which are Aces and 2 are kings.</p>\n<p>The Addition Rule for Mutually Exclusive Events:</p>\n<p>If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are mutually exclusive events, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{or}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ P}}\\left( F \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(Ace or King) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{{10}} + \\frac{2}{{10}} = \\frac{6}{{10}} = \\frac{3}{5}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 516387,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
